Description: Build with clang 16+ and GCC 14+, where incompatible function pointer types are errors: the stream wrapper functions of 0.13 took char * for the paths and modes that the php_stream_wrapper_ops of PHP 5.6 pass as const char * (the shell, exec, scp, tunnel and sftp wrappers). They take const char * now, as in ssh2 1.x, and the mode parser is static inline (a plain C99 inline that is not inlined has no definition). And ssh2.sftp://, ssh2.scp://, ssh2.exec:// with the SSH2 or SFTP resource put into the string ("ssh2.sftp://$sftp/path", the example of the documentation): since PHP 5.6.28 php_url_parse() takes the "#" of "Resource id #5" for the start of a fragment and the wrapper failed (Debian bug #848632; only intval($sftp) worked); "Resource id #" right after "://" is taken away before the parse now, so that the host is the number of the resource
Origin: azsupport; the resource in the URL: pecl-networking-ssh2 commit 093906ec1c065e86ad1cd4dabbc89b1ccae11938 (Remi Collet, 10.11.2016, branch php5, after 0.13; in ssh2 1.0 and later), as Debian (php-ssh2 0.12-3+deb8u1, debian/patches/0003-fix-for-PHP-7.0.13-where-php_url_parse-fails.patch), Remi (php-pecl-ssh2, branch php5, ssh2-php5628.patch) and Gentoo (0.13-parse_url-fix.patch) carry it, with a memmove() of the rest of the string instead of its strncpy(), whose length writes past the copy when "Resource id #" stands more than 15 characters into the URL, and only right after "://", where the host is (strstr() anywhere took a path with it in it apart)

